response.rawText:
{"text":"Yes, your body can adapt to TENS stimulation over time, which may make the sensation feel less noticeable. This a normal response called habituation. To help maintain effectiveness: Increase the intensity slightly as needed (while keeping it comfortable), Adjust pad placement between sessions, Use different modes or settings if your device offers them, Avoid using the same exact settings every time.

Useful Resources & Links:
📋 [TENS Electrode Placement Chart](https://paintechnology.s3.amazonaws.com/pdf/placementchart.pdf)"}

